course: dictionary
lesson: 4692
title: Homework and the work that counts
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Homework is school work that a pupil does at home. It is meant to help you practise and learn, so it should be your own work. «Telling a grown-up kindly about a little brother's copied homework helps him learn.» Copying does not teach you anything, and the homework does its job only when you do it yourself.
explain: Homework is also work you do before you are ready for something. Doing your homework can mean preparing well first. «She did her homework before buying a bike» means she found out what she needed to know before she bought it.
explain: When you read a word, look at the words around it. «Jayden forgot his homework completely after a big game night, owned up to his teacher, did it at lunch and missed playtime.» Here homework is the school work he had to finish, and the clues show it was important enough to give up playtime.
fact: Homework means school work that a pupil does at home.
fact: Common phrases are «do homework», «hand in homework», «maths homework» and «homework club».
fact: Homework is often counted in pages or problems, such as 3 pages of maths and 2 pages of reading.
fact: When you add homework, use «in all» to find the total. When you compare, use «how many more» to find the difference.
fact: «Homework» can also mean preparing well before something, as in «She did her homework before buying a bike».
exercise: «Jayden forgot his homework completely after a big game night, owned up to his teacher, did it at lunch and missed playtime.» What did Jayden do at lunch? | Ate a big meal | *Did his homework | Went home early | Played a game
exercise: Ana has 4 pages of maths homework and 3 pages of reading homework. How many pages in all? | 3 | 1 | *7 | 12
exercise: Ben finished 5 homework problems. Sam finished 8. How many more problems did Sam finish? | 13 | 5 | *3 | 8
test: Which phrase means giving your finished work to the teacher? | homework club | maths homework | *hand in homework | do homework
test: What does «She did her homework before buying a bike» mean? | She finished her sums at school | She did not buy anything | *She prepared and found out what she needed before buying a bike | She sold her bike
exam: In «after a row about homework», what does homework mean? | a bike | a game night | a lunch break | *school work done at home
